From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pa1q device tree <noreply@local>
Date: Wed, 24 Jul 2026 19:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] twrp: vendor unmount/flash teardown for decrypt stack

PROBLEM
  /vendor cannot be unmounted or flashed while TWRP is running. The decrypt.sh
  orchestrator mounts /vendor (erofs from mapper/vendor_a) and holds it via:
  - 5 running daemons (qseecomd, keymint, hermes, thermal, bootctl) that mmap
    .so libraries from /vendor/lib64, keeping open file handles
  - 2 nested bind mounts on top (/vendor/etc/vintf tmpfs overlay for VINTF
    manifest surgery, /vendor/firmware_mnt vfat for the modem TA image)
  
  Attempts to unmount /vendor from the Mount page fail with EBUSY. Attempts to
  flash a vendor.img fail with "block device busy" because the dm-linear device
  mapper/vendor_a is still active and mounted while the raw super partition
  underneath is being written.

FIX (additive; two hooks in partition.cpp + teardown mode in decrypt.sh)
  1. UnMount() hook: when unmounting /vendor fails (Is_Mounted() after umount2)
     AND the decrypt stack is active (/vendor/bin/qseecomd exists), trigger the
     teardown sequence (setprop twrp.decrypt.vendor_teardown 1), wait for the
     completion marker (/tmp/.vendor_freed), then retry umount2. If it succeeds
     this time, return true; otherwise fall through to the existing error path.
     
  2. Flash_Image() hook: when flashing /vendor or /vendor_image AND the decrypt
     stack is active, trigger teardown BEFORE any write operations begin. This
     frees the dm device and underlying block so the raw image write succeeds.
     
  3. decrypt.sh teardown mode (device tree, not in this patch): new property
     check at script entry. If twrp.decrypt.vendor_teardown=1, stop all decrypt
     daemons (thermal, watcher, hermes, keymint, bootctl, qseecomd, vold,
     keystore2) in reverse dependency order, unmount the nested mounts
     (/vendor/etc/vintf, /vendor/firmware_mnt), unmount /vendor, delete the
     dm vendor_a device (dmctl delete), write the completion marker
     /tmp/.vendor_freed, and exit. The vendor partition is now free for
     unmount/remount/flash by the user.
     
  Recovery: the user runs "setprop twrp.decrypt.run 1" (the existing decrypt
  trigger) to remount /vendor and restart the daemon stack. decrypt.sh is
  idempotent on the vendor mount (checks "if [ ! -e /vendor/bin/qseecomd ]")
  and hermes restarts via the two-pass protocol (WIP128 marker files) so the
  eSE Weaver slot is not touched and biometric unlock remains functional.

  Files (for revert): bootable/recovery/partition.cpp
                      device tree: recovery/root/system/bin/decrypt.sh
---
diff --git a/partition.cpp b/partition.cpp
--- a/partition.cpp	2026-07-24 19:06:13.919852227 +0300
+++ b/partition.cpp	2026-07-24 19:20:42.291715906 +0300
@@ -1750,6 +1750,22 @@
 
 		umount2(Mount_Point.c_str(), flags);
 		if (Is_Mounted()) {
+		// WIP131: vendor teardown if busy and held by decrypt daemons
+		if (Mount_Point == "/vendor" && TWFunc::Path_Exists("/vendor/bin/qseecomd")) {
+			gui_msg("vendor_teardown=Vendor held by decrypt - releasing...");
+			unlink("/tmp/.vendor_freed");  // clear stale marker before triggering
+			TWFunc::Exec_Cmd("setprop twrp.decrypt.vendor_teardown 1");
+			// Wait for teardown completion marker
+			int wait = 0;
+			while (wait < 100 && !TWFunc::Path_Exists("/tmp/.vendor_freed")) {
+				usleep(100000);  // 0.1s
+				wait++;
+			}
+			// Retry unmount after teardown
+			umount2(Mount_Point.c_str(), flags);
+		}
+		// Check again after potential vendor teardown
+		if (Is_Mounted()) {
 			if (Display_Error)
 				gui_msg(Msg(msg::kError, "fail_unmount=Failed to unmount '{1}' ({2})")(Mount_Point)(strerror(errno)));
 			else
@@ -3303,6 +3319,22 @@
 
 	LOGINFO("Image filename is: %s\n", Backup_FileName.c_str());
 
+	// WIP131: vendor teardown before flashing - free the block device
+	if ((Mount_Point == "/vendor" || Mount_Point == "/vendor_image") 
+	    && TWFunc::Path_Exists("/vendor/bin/qseecomd")) {
+		gui_msg("vendor_teardown_flash=Releasing vendor for flashing...");
+		unlink("/tmp/.vendor_freed");  // clear stale marker before triggering
+		TWFunc::Exec_Cmd("setprop twrp.decrypt.vendor_teardown 1");
+		// Wait for teardown completion
+		int wait = 0;
+		while (wait < 100 && !TWFunc::Path_Exists("/tmp/.vendor_freed")) {
+			usleep(100000);  // 0.1s
+			wait++;
+		}
+		LOGINFO("Vendor teardown completed (wait=%d)
+", wait);
+	}
+
 	if (Backup_Method == BM_FILES) {
 		LOGERR("Cannot flash images to file systems\n");
 		return false;
